From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 04:57:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: Disable ASPM L0s for SM8475 PCIe0

On the Xiaomi 12T Pro (SM8475) the QCA6490 is on PCIe0. The kernel enables
ASPM L0s and L1 on the links of a devicetree platform by default, and with
L0s on this link reports correctable errors: Replay Timer Timeout in the
Wi-Fi chip and Bad TLP in the root port. They follow how often the link
leaves its low-power states, not the amount of data. Six downloads of
100 MB with pauses between them gave none; 4 MB transfers with gaps of 30
to 100 ms gave 11 errors in 300 s with L0s enabled (the same with the L1
substates off) and none in 200 s with ASPM disabled through the policy.

The stock device tree of the phone says the platform does not support L0s
(qcom,no-l0s-supported). Upstream disables it for sc8280xp, sa8540p and
sa8295p for the same errors on the same Wi-Fi chip ("PCI: qcom: Disable
ASPM L0s for sc8280xp, sa8540p and sa8295p"): Qualcomm confirmed that the
PHY configuration of those platforms is not tuned for L0s.

Give SM8475 PCIe0 its own compatible and configuration, as sc8280xp has.
L1 and the L1 substates stay on.

Signed-off-by: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/qcom,pcie-sm8450.yaml | 1 +
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi                         | 7 +++++++
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c                      | 6 ++++++
 3 files changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/qcom,pcie-sm8450.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/qcom,pcie-sm8450.yaml
index 28b8ffb..804f42a 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/qcom,pcie-sm8450.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/qcom,pcie-sm8450.yaml
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@ properties:
     enum:
       - qcom,pcie-sm8450-pcie0
       - qcom,pcie-sm8450-pcie1
+      - qcom,pcie-sm8475-pcie0
 
   reg:
     minItems: 5
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi
index 2f5b29b..9a18b5b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi
@@ -65,8 +65,14 @@
  * MSIs from the endpoint never reach the GIC ITS on SM8475 (the vendor kernel
  * uses SPI-based MSI as well): ath11k's MHI boot times out. Use the
  * controller's own MSI interrupts.
+ *
+ * ASPM L0s stays off, as in the vendor device tree (qcom,no-l0s-supported):
+ * with it on, the link to the QCA6490 reports correctable errors (BadTLP,
+ * Timeout). The compatible selects the driver configuration without L0s.
  */
 &pcie0 {
+	compatible = "qcom,pcie-sm8475-pcie0";
+
 	/delete-property/ msi-map;
 	/delete-property/ msi-map-mask;
 };
diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
index d62cf30..b00cdff 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -1573,6 +1573,12 @@ static const struct qcom_pcie_cfg cfg_1_9_0 = {
 	.ops = &ops_1_9_0,
 };
 
+/* SM8475 PCIe0: 1.9.0 with ASPM L0s off (the PHY is not tuned for it) */
+static const struct qcom_pcie_cfg cfg_sm8475_pcie0 = {
+	.ops = &ops_1_9_0,
+	.no_l0s = true,
+};
+
 static const struct qcom_pcie_cfg cfg_1_34_0 = {
 	.ops = &ops_1_9_0,
 	.override_no_snoop = true,
@@ -2344,6 +2350,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_pcie_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,pcie-sm8350", .data = &cfg_1_9_0 },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,pcie-sm8450-pcie0", .data = &cfg_1_9_0 },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,pcie-sm8450-pcie1", .data = &cfg_1_9_0 },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,pcie-sm8475-pcie0", .data = &cfg_sm8475_pcie0 },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,pcie-sm8550", .data = &cfg_1_9_0 },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,pcie-x1e80100", .data = &cfg_sc8280xp },
 	{ }
